---@field nluIntentConfidenceThreshold? aws.lex_model_building_service.ConfidenceThreshold The score that determines where Amazon Lex inserts the AMAZON.FallbackIntent, AMAZON.KendraSearchIntent, or both when returning alternative intents in a PostContent or PostText response. AMAZON.FallbackIntent is inserted if the confidence score for all intents is below this value. AMAZON.KendraSearchIntent is only inserted if it is configured for the bot.
---@field clarificationPrompt? aws.lex_model_building_service.Prompt The prompts that Amazon Lex uses when it doesn't understand the user's intent. For more information, see PutBot.
---@field abortStatement? aws.lex_model_building_service.Statement The message that Amazon Lex uses to cancel a conversation. For more information, see PutBot.
---@field status? aws.lex_model_building_service.Status When you send a request to create a bot with processBehavior set to BUILD, Amazon Lex sets the status response element to BUILDING.
---@field failureReason? aws.lex_model_building_service.String If status is FAILED, Amazon Lex provides the reason that it failed to build the bot.
