---@field createdDate? aws.lex_model_building_service.Timestamp The date that the bot was created.
---@field idleSessionTTLInSeconds? aws.lex_model_building_service.SessionTTL The maximum length of time that Amazon Lex retains the data gathered in a conversation. For more information, see PutBot.
---@field voiceId? aws.lex_model_building_service.String The Amazon Polly voice ID that Amazon Lex uses for voice interaction with the user. For more information, see PutBot.
---@field checksum? aws.lex_model_building_service.String Checksum of the bot that you created.
---@field version? aws.lex_model_building_service.Version The version of the bot. For a new bot, the version is always $LATEST.
---@field locale? aws.lex_model_building_service.Locale The target locale for the bot.
---@field childDirected? aws.lex_model_building_service.Boolean For each Amazon Lex bot created with the Amazon Lex Model Building Service, you must specify whether your use of Amazon Lex is related to a website, program, or other application that is directed or targeted, in whole or in part, to children under age 13 and subject to the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) by specifying true or false in the childDirected field. By specifying true in...
---@field createVersion? aws.lex_model_building_service.Boolean True if a new version of the bot was created. If the createVersion field was not specified in the request, the createVersion field is set to false in the response.
---@field detectSentiment? aws.lex_model_building_service.Boolean true if the bot is configured to send user utterances to Amazon Comprehend for sentiment analysis. If the detectSentiment field was not specified in the request, the detectSentiment field is false in the response.
