---@class aws.lex_model_building_service.PutIntentRequest
---@field name aws.lex_model_building_service.IntentName The name of the intent. The name is not case sensitive.
---@field description? aws.lex_model_building_service.Description A description of the intent.
---@field slots? aws.lex_model_building_service.SlotList An array of intent slots. At runtime, Amazon Lex elicits required slot values from the user using prompts defined in the slots. For more information, see how-it-works.
---@field sampleUtterances? aws.lex_model_building_service.IntentUtteranceList An array of utterances (strings) that a user might say to signal the intent. For example, "I want {PizzaSize} pizza", "Order {Quantity} {PizzaSize} pizzas".
---@field confirmationPrompt? aws.lex_model_building_service.Prompt Prompts the user to confirm the intent. This question should have a yes or no answer.
---@field rejectionStatement? aws.lex_model_building_service.Statement When the user answers "no" to the question defined in confirmationPrompt, Amazon Lex responds with this statement to acknowledge that the intent was canceled.
---@field followUpPrompt? aws.lex_model_building_service.FollowUpPrompt Amazon Lex uses this prompt to solicit additional activity after fulfilling an intent. For example, after the OrderPizza intent is fulfilled, you might prompt the user to order a drink.
---@field conclusionStatement? aws.lex_model_building_service.Statement The statement that you want Amazon Lex to convey to the user after the intent is successfully fulfilled by the Lambda function.
---@field dialogCodeHook? aws.lex_model_building_service.CodeHook Specifies a Lambda function to invoke for each user input. You can invoke this Lambda function to personalize user interaction.
---@field fulfillmentActivity? aws.lex_model_building_service.FulfillmentActivity Required. Describes how the intent is fulfilled. For example, after a user provides all of the information for a pizza order, fulfillmentActivity defines how the bot places an order with a local pizza store.
---@field parentIntentSignature? aws.lex_model_building_service.BuiltinIntentSignature A unique identifier for the built-in intent to base this intent on. To find the signature for an intent, see Standard Built-in Intents in the Alexa Skills Kit.
---@field checksum? aws.lex_model_building_service.String Identifies a specific revision of the $LATEST version.
---@field createVersion? aws.lex_model_building_service.Boolean When set to true a new numbered version of the intent is created. This is the same as calling the CreateIntentVersion operation. If you do not specify createVersion, the default is false.
---@field kendraConfiguration? aws.lex_model_building_service.KendraConfiguration Configuration information required to use the AMAZON.KendraSearchIntent intent to connect to an Amazon Kendra index. For more information, see AMAZON.KendraSearchIntent.
---@field inputContexts? aws.lex_model_building_service.InputContextList An array of InputContext objects that lists the contexts that must be active for Amazon Lex to choose the intent in a conversation with the user.
---@field outputContexts? aws.lex_model_building_service.OutputContextList An array of OutputContext objects that lists the contexts that the intent activates when the intent is fulfilled.

